Mini Project : 📚 Library Book Management System

📌 Brief Description

The Library Book Management System is a file-based C++ application for managing library book records.

The system stores important book information such as ISBN, title, author, category, and availability in a text file.

It can provide operations for adding, searching, issuing, returning, updating books, and generating an availability report.

🔑 Key Concepts

- 📄 Text-file handling
- 💾 Persistent data storage
- ➕ Adding book records
- 🔍 Searching book records
- 📤 Issuing books
- 📥 Returning books
- ✏️ Updating records
- 📊 Generating availability reports

🌍 Real-World Application

This project can be used as the foundation of a school, college, or public library management system where book information must be stored and retrieved persistently.

🎯 Main Purpose

To combine C++ file-handling concepts into a practical application that manages library records efficiently.

🚀 Main Features

- ➕ Add a new book
- 🔎 Search for a book
- 📤 Issue a book
- 📥 Return a book
- ✏️ Update book details
- 📊 Generate an availability report
